  "version": "1.28.4",
  "notes": "**Coding agents no longer silently delete code when they edit a file.**\n\n- **Fixed:** some models, such as DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, send the edit tool's replacement text under their own field name. ChatOSS didn't recognize it, treated the replacement as empty, and deleted the text it was supposed to replace. The agent was still told \"Edited\", so the damage went unnoticed. Those edits now land as intended. An edit that arrives without any replacement text is now refused with a clear error, and nothing is deleted.\n- **Fixed:** replacement text containing `$'`, `$$` or `$&` (common in SQL, shell scripts and JavaScript template strings) was altered on the way into the file, and could duplicate the rest of the file. Agents' edits are now written exactly as they wrote them.\n- **Fixed:** a file write that arrived without any contents emptied the file. It is now refused and the file is left alone.\n\nThis affects the Code, Create and Orchestrate agents.\n",
